React Native 0.88: build the Android text input's props and state off Android.

AndroidTextInputProps declares getDiffProps and getDiffPropsImplementationTarget
as overrides of Props methods that exist only with RN_SERIALIZABLE_STATE, and
its getDynamic converts colours with the Android-only toAndroidRepr.
AndroidTextInputState's dynamic constructor, getDynamic and getMapBuffer are
the same serialisation, which ConcreteState only uses with
RN_SERIALIZABLE_STATE. Other components (Text, RawText, Image,
UnimplementedView, the Android paragraph props, ScrollViewState) guard this
API with #ifdef RN_SERIALIZABLE_STATE; this patch adds the same guard, so the
shared props, state and shadow node build on hosts without Android's
serialisation (the OxyOS host). Behaviour with RN_SERIALIZABLE_STATE (Android) is unchanged.

Upstream (facebook/react-native main) still lacks the guard at the time of
writing. build.sh applies this to a private copy of the module in its work
directory; the React Native package itself is never modified.

